{
  "result": "If I could change one thing, I'd make being wrong feel like discovery instead of defeat.\n\nNot make people smarter, or kinder, or make everyone agree \u2014 just lower the sting of *oh, I had that wrong.*\n\nSo much gets stuck there. An argument stops being about what's true and becomes about not losing face. An apology gets delayed for years because admitting it hurts. A scientist defends an old theory, a parent doubles down, a whole country can't course-correct, not because the evidence isn't there, but because updating feels like humiliation.\n\nImagine if that moment \u2014 realizing you misunderstood someone, or a fact, or yourself \u2014 came with curiosity first. A little *oh, interesting* before the shame.\n\nPeople would still argue, still believe incompatible things, still make terrible decisions sometimes. But they'd recover faster. They'd listen longer. They'd let experiences actually teach them.\n\nMost of the damage I see in human stories isn't from not knowing. It's from needing not to find out.",
